1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,417
Ava: KV Cache reuse can cut prefill work, but moving that cache also costs time.
Ava：复用 KV Cache 能减少预填充计算，但搬运缓存也需要时间。

2
00:00:06,417 --> 00:00:15,494
KVCache Meetup Korea 2026 put that trade-off beside GPU bottlenecks, scheduling, and cache management.
KVCache Meetup Korea 2026 将这一取舍与 GPU 瓶颈、调度和缓存管理放在一起讨论。

3
00:00:15,494 --> 00:00:26,700
Brian: PyTorchKR and XCENA co-hosted the event on Sep 30, 2026, with sponsorship from Tensormesh.
Brian：PyTorchKR 和 XCENA 于 2026 年 9 月 30 日联合举办了这场活动，由 Tensormesh 赞助。

4
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:34,396
Speakers came from XCENA, SK hynix, FuriosaAI, and LMCache.
演讲者来自 XCENA、SK hynix、FuriosaAI 和 LMCache。

5
00:00:34,396 --> 00:00:38,734
Ava: Let's start with CXL. So capacity is only part of it.
Ava：先说 CXL。容量只是其中一方面。

6
00:00:38,734 --> 00:00:44,322
The inference engine still needs to get useful cache to the GPU.
推理引擎还得把有用的缓存送到 GPU。

7
00:00:44,322 --> 00:00:52,832
Brian: Jooho Lee explained that CXL expands the memory space CPUs can access with load and store instructions.
Brian：Jooho Lee 解释说，CXL 扩展了 CPU 可通过加载和存储指令访问的内存空间。

8
00:00:52,832 --> 00:00:56,550
He described a pool shared by multiple hosts.
他介绍了一个由多台主机共享的内存池。

9
00:00:56,550 --> 00:01:03,408
Frequently used cache stays in DRAM, while less frequently used cache goes on SSDs.
常用缓存留在 DRAM，不常用的则放到 SSD 上。

10
00:01:03,408 --> 00:01:10,679
XCENA's open-source storage engine, Maru, connects the inference engine to those layers.
XCENA 的开源存储引擎 Maru 将推理引擎与这些存储层连接起来。

11
00:01:10,679 --> 00:01:15,656
The path and cost of moving cache to the GPU matter too.
缓存送往 GPU 的路径和搬运成本也很重要。

12
00:01:15,656 --> 00:01:22,007
Ava: The talk also covered splitting mixture-of-experts work between a GPU and MX1.
Ava：演讲还谈到如何让 GPU 和 MX1 分担混合专家模型的工作。

13
00:01:22,007 --> 00:01:27,462
Some expert weights sit in memory near MX1 and are processed there.
部分专家权重存放在 MX1 附近的内存中，并由 MX1 处理。

14
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:33,430
The design transfers activations and results instead of full weights.
这种设计传输的是激活值和结果，而非完整权重。

15
00:01:33,430 --> 00:01:38,449
Brian: Sejin Oh looked at GPU compute and HBM bandwidth.
Brian：Sejin Oh 考察了 GPU 算力和 HBM 带宽。

16
00:01:38,449 --> 00:01:44,492
The experiments used two H100 GPUs, Llama 3.1 8B, and vLLM.
实验使用了两块 H100 GPU、Llama 3.1 8B 和 vLLM。

17
00:01:44,492 --> 00:01:52,072
GPU compute use was high during the main projection operations in prefill.
预填充阶段的主要投影运算对 GPU 算力的利用率很高。

18
00:01:52,072 --> 00:01:56,724
During decode, HBM bandwidth use was high.
解码阶段的 HBM 带宽利用率很高。

19
00:01:56,724 --> 00:02:01,920
Ava: That helps explain why reusing KV Cache can change the bottleneck.
Ava：这有助于解释为什么复用 KV Cache 会改变瓶颈所在。

20
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:08,018
If prefill needs less computation, memory bandwidth can become the limit.
如果预填充所需计算减少，内存带宽就可能成为限制。

21
00:02:08,018 --> 00:02:19,049
Brian: Whether a service needs more memory capacity or bandwidth depends on input and output lengths, batch size, and other operating conditions.
Brian：服务更需要内存容量还是带宽，取决于输入和输出长度、批量大小等运行条件。

22
00:02:19,049 --> 00:02:26,992
The talk also separated TTFT, time to the first output token, from TPOT, time per output token.
演讲还区分了 TTFT（首个输出 token 的生成时间）和 TPOT（每个输出 token 的生成时间）。

23
00:02:26,992 --> 00:02:33,867
Ava: Donghun Lee's FuriosaAI talk moved from resource limits to request scheduling on RNGD.
Ava：Donghun Lee 在 FuriosaAI 的演讲中，将话题从资源限制转向了 RNGD 上的请求调度。

24
00:02:33,867 --> 00:02:37,974
He followed requests from arrival to execution.
他梳理了请求从到达到执行的过程。

25
00:02:37,974 --> 00:02:47,583
Brian: He covered PagedAttention for KV Cache blocks, Continuous batching for active requests, and Chunked prefill for smaller prompt segments.
Brian：他介绍了用于 KV Cache 块的 PagedAttention、处理活跃请求的 Continuous batching，以及将提示词拆成小段的 Chunked prefill。

26
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:53,444
He also introduced buckets, which are tensor shapes compiled before execution.
他还介绍了 bucket，即执行前预先编译的张量形状。

27
00:02:53,444 --> 00:03:00,544
Ava: Combining requests can raise throughput, but a larger batch may need a larger bucket and add latency.
Ava：合并请求能提高吞吐量，但更大的批量可能需要更大的 bucket，从而增加延迟。

28
00:03:00,544 --> 00:03:03,706
Padding in a fixed shape has a cost too.
固定形状下的填充也有开销。

29
00:03:03,706 --> 00:03:07,660
Brian: Furiosa-LLM measures execution cost on the actual hardware.
Brian：Furiosa-LLM 在实际硬件上测量执行成本。

30
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:18,600
It merges two batches when their combined cost is lower than processing them separately, accounting for each request's context length and the cost of padding.
考虑每个请求的上下文长度和填充成本后，如果合并执行的成本低于分别处理，它就会合并两个批次。

31
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:23,146
Ava: What about the cost of retrieving cache instead of recomputing it?
Ava：取回缓存与重新计算相比，成本如何？

32
00:03:23,146 --> 00:03:25,838
The talk compared those two paths.
演讲比较了这两种方式。

33
00:03:25,838 --> 00:03:34,408
Brian: The slides used a 12,370-token prompt, one request at a time, and three measurements for each condition.
Brian：幻灯片中的测试使用了 12,370 个 token 的提示词，每次处理一个请求，每种条件测量三次。

34
00:03:34,408 --> 00:03:49,756
Retrieving the host cache and generating the first token took about 92 ms. Recomputing the cache took about 900 ms. Under those test conditions, retrieving the host cache was faster.
取回主机缓存并生成首个 token 约需 92 毫秒；重新计算缓存约需 900 毫秒。在这些测试条件下，取回主机缓存更快。

35
00:03:49,756 --> 00:03:54,701
Ava: The benefit depends on how much data moves and the available bandwidth.
Ava：收益取决于传输的数据量和可用带宽。

36
00:03:54,701 --> 00:04:00,064
The talk described overlapping cache transfer with computation at each layer.
演讲介绍了如何在每一层让缓存传输与计算重叠进行。

37
00:04:00,064 --> 00:04:07,866
Experimental features included a network-shared cache and running prefill and decode on separate resources.
实验性功能包括网络共享缓存，以及让预填充和解码使用不同的资源。

38
00:04:07,866 --> 00:04:11,276
Brian: Baoloong Mao's LMCache talk focused on MP Mode.
Brian：Baoloong Mao 的 LMCache 演讲聚焦 MP Mode。

39
00:04:11,276 --> 00:04:17,225
It moves cache management out of the inference engine and into a separate process.
它将缓存管理从推理引擎移到独立进程。

40
00:04:17,225 --> 00:04:23,960
That separates inference computation from cache I/O to reduce competition for resources.
这样能将推理计算与缓存 I/O 分开，减少资源争用。

41
00:04:23,960 --> 00:04:27,131
Ava: The processes still need to coordinate.
Ava：这些进程仍需相互协调。

42
00:04:27,131 --> 00:04:35,206
They exchange control information such as block IDs, while CUDA IPC lets them share GPU memory.
它们交换块 ID 等控制信息，并通过 CUDA IPC 共享 GPU 内存。

43
00:04:35,206 --> 00:04:41,191
Brian: Within a node, they use a shared CPU memory pool to reduce duplicate storage.
Brian：在同一节点内，它们使用共享 CPU 内存池来减少重复存储。

44
00:04:41,191 --> 00:04:47,292
MP Mode also reads and loads data from several storage layers in parallel.
MP Mode 还能并行读取和加载多个存储层的数据。

45
00:04:47,292 --> 00:04:49,909
Ava: The operations side matters as well.
Ava：运维方面也很重要。

46
00:04:49,909 --> 00:05:00,074
The talk covered Kubernetes deployment, cache hit rates, cache lifetimes, and isolating failures between inference and cache processes.
演讲涉及 Kubernetes 部署、缓存命中率、缓存存活时间，以及推理进程与缓存进程之间的故障隔离。

47
00:05:00,074 --> 00:05:09,443
Brian: In the Q&A, attendees asked about separating prefill and decode compared with mixed batching, which processes them together.
Brian：问答环节中，听众询问了分离预填充与解码，和将两者一起处理的混合批处理有何区别。

48
00:05:09,443 --> 00:05:18,256
They also asked about LMCache alongside vLLM's built-in cache features and plans to extend MP Mode across nodes.
他们还问到 LMCache 如何与 vLLM 内置的缓存功能配合，以及将 MP Mode 扩展到跨节点的计划。

49
00:05:18,256 --> 00:05:21,158
Ava: The event included time to connect.
Ava：活动也安排了交流时间。

50
00:05:21,158 --> 00:05:30,860
At registration, attendees could choose up to two interest stickers from Model, Serving, Infra, Hardware, and Memory.
签到时，参加者可以从 Model、Serving、Infra、Hardware 和 Memory 中选择最多两张兴趣贴纸。

51
00:05:30,860 --> 00:05:37,926
They later gathered in small groups and examined XCENA's CXL server at the venue.
随后，他们分成小组，在现场查看了 XCENA 的 CXL 服务器。

52
00:05:37,926 --> 00:05:42,953
Brian: The feedback summary was based on 72 survey responses.
Brian：反馈总结基于 72 份问卷答复。

53
00:05:42,953 --> 00:05:53,287
In a question that allowed multiple selections, 48 respondents chose the program as a positive point, or 66.7%.
在一道多选题中，48 人将活动议程选为亮点，占 66.7%。

54
00:05:53,287 --> 00:05:59,036
The venue and facilities received 30 selections, or 41.7%.
场地和设施获得 30 票，占 41.7%。

55
00:05:59,036 --> 00:06:06,386
Ava: Respondents raised microphone quality and volume, screen visibility from the back rows, and limited space.
Ava：受访者提到麦克风音质和音量、后排看不清屏幕，以及空间有限等问题。

56
00:06:06,386 --> 00:06:10,824
Some wanted interpretation or translation for the English talks.
一些人希望英语演讲能提供口译或翻译。

57
00:06:10,824 --> 00:06:16,930
Others asked for a dedicated session where developers in the same field could talk.
还有人希望设置专场，让同领域的开发者交流。

58
00:06:16,930 --> 00:06:28,910
Brian: For future events, respondents asked for real production examples, vLLM and SGLang internals, NPU compilers, recent inference optimization techniques, and demos.
Brian：对于今后的活动，受访者希望看到真实的生产案例、vLLM 和 SGLang 的内部机制、NPU 编译器、最新的推理优化技术，以及演示。

59
00:06:28,910 --> 00:06:38,359
Across these talks, cache capacity, transfer cost, compute, bandwidth, and scheduling all shaped the discussion of LLM serving.
这些演讲围绕 LLM 服务展开讨论，缓存容量、传输成本、算力、带宽和调度都是关键因素。

60
00:06:38,359 --> 00:06:40,272
Thanks for listening.
感谢收听。
